-- title:
--   Fontaine's membership criterion for truncated Witt covectors
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring in which the image of $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, and let $k$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra such that the structure map $\mathcal O \to k$ is surjective with kernel exactly the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-bialgebra which is flat as an $\mathcal O$-module, let $n$ be a natural number, and put $A = k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R$, a bialgebra over $k$. Let $a$ be a truncated Witt vector of length $n$ over $A$ satisfying two hypotheses. First, $a$ lies in [`Deformation.TruncWitt.fontaineKer`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L76) for the ring homomorphism $\mathcal R \to A$, $r \mapsto 1 \otimes r$: there is a Witt vector $X$ over $\mathcal R$ whose image in $W(A)$ truncates at level $n$ to $a$ and whose $(n-1)$-st ghost component lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$. Second, the Verschiebung of $a$ (the shift on truncated Witt vectors) lies in [`Deformation.wittHom`](def/Dieudonne_WittVectorHom.html#L246), i.e. applying $W_n$ to the comultiplication $A \to A \otimes_k A$ gives the same result as the sum of the images under $W_n$ of the two inclusions $A \to A \otimes_k A$. The conclusion is that $a$ itself satisfies this last, "homomorphism", condition.
--
--   This is the criterion, at the finite level $W_n$, with which Fontaine's description of the Dieudonné module of a finite flat commutative group scheme begins: a Witt covector on the special fibre that is killed by the map $w$ and whose Verschiebung is a homomorphism is already a homomorphism. It is used in the deduction of the structural statements about the Dieudonné module recorded in [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_add_eq_of_smul_eq_zero`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_add_eq_of_smul_eq_zero), [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_frobenius_eq_smul`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_frobenius_eq_smul) and [`Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_verschiebung_eq_of_frobenius_eq_zero`](thm.html#Deformation.DieudonneModule.exists_mem_fontaineHodge_verschiebung_eq_of_frobenius_eq_zero).
-- source:
